{"name":"Calm Air","hex":"#eed2ae","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"calm","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Peaceful, quiet, especially free from anger and anxiety.","Free of noise and disturbance."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state of being calm; peacefulness; absence of worry, anger, fear or other strong negative emotion.","The state of being calm; absence of noise and disturbance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calm"},{"term":"air","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Airoran."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The substance constituting Earth's atmosphere: a gaseous mixture of nitrogen, oxygen, and various trace gases.","The substance of the atmosphere seen as an agency of freshness."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/air"}],"entries":[{"title":"Calm Air","blocks":[{"text":"Calm Air International LP. is a full service airline, offering passenger, charter and freight services in northern Manitoba and the Kivalliq Region of Nunavut. It is owned by Exchange Income Corporation with its main base in Winnipeg, Manitoba."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/C-FAFS_AT43_Calm_Air_Cambridge_Bay.JPG/330px-C-FAFS_AT43_Calm_Air_Cambridge_Bay.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calm_Air"},{"title":"Atmosphere of Earth","blocks":[{"text":"The atmosphere of Earth consists of a layer of mixed gas that is retained by gravity, surrounding the Earth's surface. It contains variable quantities of suspended aerosols and particulates that create weather features such as clouds and hazes. The atmosphere serves as a protective buffer between the Earth's surface and outer space. It shields the surface from most meteoroids and ultraviolet solar radiation, reduces diurnal temperature variation – the temperature extremes between day and night, and keeps it warm through heat retention via the greenhouse effect. The atmosphere redistributes heat and moisture among different regions via air currents, and provides the chemical and climate conditions that allow life to exist and evolve on Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Top_of_Atmosphere.jpg/330px-Top_of_Atmosphere.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atmosphere_of_Earth"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Calm_Air_C-GTJY_Saab.jpg/500px-Calm_Air_C-GTJY_Saab.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Calm_Air_C-GTJY_Saab.jpg/500px-Calm_Air_C-GTJY_Saab.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" A Saab 340 operated by Calm Air in 2007","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACalm_Air_C-GTJY_Saab.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Calm_Air_C_FECI.jpg/500px-Calm_Air_C_FECI.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Calm_Air_C_FECI.jpg/1280px-Calm_Air_C_FECI.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Calm_Air_C_FECI.jpg/500px-Calm_Air_C_FECI.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Calm Air ATR 42 at Winnipeg airport","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACalm_Air_C_FECI.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/ISS-46_Soyuz_TMA-17M_reentry.jpg/500px-ISS-46_Soyuz_TMA-17M_reentry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/ISS-46_Soyuz_TMA-17M_reentry.jpg/1280px-ISS-46_Soyuz_TMA-17M_reentry.jpg?